为什么这对她行不通？

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:42.799
She says that like dudes are such chicks, like the idea that she just perceives this neediness on the, she sees it as neediness, right?
她说男人就像小鸡一样，她认为她只是察觉到了对方的渴求，她把它看作是渴求，对吧？

00:18:42.799 --> 00:18:44.279
This person wanted to connect with her.
这个人想和她建立联系。

00:18:44.279 --> 00:18:46.039
She says that is sort of needy and weak.
她说那是一种渴求和软弱。

00:18:46.039 --> 00:18:51.079
And I love that in a series television, you have the chance to explore why.
我喜欢在电视剧里，你有机会去探索原因。

00:18:51.079 --> 00:18:54.799
When you extend the timeline forward, and maybe we didn't even know at the time.
当你把时间线往后推，也许我们当时甚至不知道。

00:18:54.799 --> 00:19:07.400
We were, we had a hint of it, we knew some ideas, but as you go and I don't want to do spoilers, we're trying not to do too much of that episode of episode, but as you go deeper in the series, you see us trying to dig deeper into her psyche and say, why is she like that?
我们当时有一点暗示，我们知道一些想法，但随着剧情深入，我们尽量不去剧透每一集，但随着系列深入，你看到我们试图挖掘她的内心，问为什么她是那样的？

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:11.920
And we learned things about her own father and her upbringing in Canada and who she was.
我们了解了关于她父亲、她在加拿大的成长经历以及她是谁的事情。

