Yes.
是的。

00:19:51.012 --> 00:19:58.315
Like the woman is going to want all the those things and the man's going to be like, you know, I want my freedom.
就像女人会想要所有那些东西，而男人会说，你知道，我想要我的自由。

00:19:58.315 --> 00:20:03.291
But I think what you guys were exploring and I don't think you invented this.
但我认为你们当时在探索的东西，我不认为这是你们发明的。

00:20:03.291 --> 00:20:13.761
I think you I think Carter was riffing on his own hopes and dreams and you certainly, you know said yes to a relationship and a marriage like on the younger side.
我觉得卡特是在即兴发挥他自己的希望和梦想，而且你确实，你知道，在比较年轻的时候就答应了一段关系和婚姻。

00:20:13.761 --> 00:20:21.128
So I think that that they're the amount of guys I hear from who say like I'm just like pet like I'm really I feel.
所以我认为，我听到的那些说“我简直就像泰德，我真的感觉……”的男人们的数量。

00:20:21.128 --> 00:20:33.408
I think that I think that you were satisfying like a market demand for like a more emotionally centered community of vulnerable men who yeah who weren't just just interested in getting laid.
我觉得你们满足了市场需求，即需要一个更以情感为中心、更脆弱的男性群体，他们不仅仅是对发生性关系感兴趣。

00:20:33.408 --> 00:20:40.905
