I mean, I remember just to go back to not us for a second.
我的意思是，我记得，先暂时跳过我们。

00:30:31.380 --> 00:30:37.940
I remember the feeling that, so there was a really cool indie rock radio station in LA.
我记得那种感觉，洛杉矶有一个非常酷的独立摇滚电台。

00:30:37.940 --> 00:30:39.700
It's 103-1, I'm forgetting the name of it.
是103.1，我忘了它的名字了。

00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:44.140
Someone sent in what the name of that was because it went off the air while I still in LA.
有人发来过它的名字，因为它在我还在洛杉矶时就停播了。

00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:51.900
But I got a bunch of great, how I met your mother's songs from that radio station, including Inside of Love by Nautacer, which I heard for the first time on that station.
但我从那个电台得到了很多《老爸老妈浪漫史》的歌曲，包括Nautacer的《Inside of Love》，我第一次听到它就是在那个电台。

00:30:51.900 --> 00:30:53.019
This is how long ago it was.
这就是很久以前的事了。

00:30:53.019 --> 00:30:56.779
We drove around in cars listening to Restreo radio stations.
我们开着车，听着地面电台。

00:30:56.779 --> 00:31:03.299
And I remember finding that song and coming to our music supervisor, Andy Galen, He also had amazing suggestions himself.
我记得发现了那首歌，并找到我们的音乐总监安迪·盖伦，他自己也有很棒的建议。

00:31:03.299 --> 00:31:14.099
This one was just because I fell in love with the song in the radio and it's saying to him, can we get this song and put it under the whole ending of this episode and he was like, yes we can.
这一首纯粹是因为我在电台爱上了这首歌，并对他说，我们能拿到这首歌并把它放在这一集的结尾吗？他说，是的，我们可以。

00:31:14.099 --> 00:31:30.940
And I remember that we got it, the song aired and I remember like this is all a long way I mentioned your question out which is to say I remember the giddy-ness I felt watching that one air and going, that's because I heard this cool song in the radio and I said, let's put it on a TV episode And now it's airing.
我记得我们拿到了它，歌曲播出了，我记得——这离你的问题有点远——我想说的是，我记得看着那一集播出时感到的那种眩晕感，心想，那是因为我在电台听到了这首酷歌，我说，把它放在电视剧里吧，现在它播出了。

00:31:30.940 --> 00:31:36.420
And I was just like one of, I just remember that giddy kind of Christmas morning feeling about that one.
我当时就像，我只记得那种像圣诞节早晨一样的眩晕感。

00:31:36.420 --> 00:31:45.420
So we were still in those new days, where those superpowers of those moments were still like, all of a sudden you could fly, all of a sudden, you know, there was just the same.
所以我们还处于那些新奇的日子里，那些时刻的超能力依然存在，就像你突然可以飞了，突然间，你知道，感觉是一样的。

00:31:45.420 --> 00:31:49.059
And if you couldn't do it, there were 12 people that could get it done for you.
如果你做不到，还有12个人可以为你完成。

00:31:49.059 --> 00:31:49.900
That's the one thing.
这就是那件事。

00:31:49.900 --> 00:31:52.740
I remember feeling, I think I was still quite nervous.
我记得那种感觉，我想我当时还是很紧张。

00:31:52.740 --> 00:32:03.779
I think I was still, it really took me a while to relax into the fact that this was a job that was gonna be a long time, long-term job, you know.
我想我还是，我真的花了一段时间才放松下来，接受这是一份会做很久的长期工作。

00:32:05.339 --> 00:32:19.539
And remember, we were not out of the gate like a ratings juggernaut, like we were in the demo, we were very good for CBS for a young audience, but our total numbers, it took a while.
而且记得，我们刚开始并不是收视率巨头，我们在目标人群中，对于哥伦比亚广播公司（CBS）的年轻观众来说表现很好，但我们的总人数，花了一段时间才上来。

00:32:19.539 --> 00:32:20.700
It's good, yeah.
很好，是的。

00:32:20.700 --> 00:32:25.539
We stayed around on the success of like 18 to 34.
我们靠着18到34岁人群的成功维持了下来。

00:32:25.539 --> 00:32:29.859
We were the youngest skewing show off and on CBS, on a given week or month, three year.
在任何一周或一个月、三年里，我们都是CBS收视群体最年轻的节目。

00:32:29.859 --> 00:32:34.539
And that is what, that's what got us, yeah, we did not, we were no huge hit, that's true.
这就是让我们坚持下来的原因，是的，我们并没有，我们不是什么巨大的热门，这是真的。

00:32:34.539 --> 00:32:35.900
It was not right advocate.
那不是理所当然的。

00:32:35.900 --> 00:32:38.420
And I was worried, I was definitely always, I remember always being worried.
我很担心，我绝对一直，我记得我总是很担心。

00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:39.579
Are these numbers good enough?
这些数字够好吗？

00:32:41.099 --> 00:33:00.380
But you know, the arc we had, which is, I think what happened was, and I think we might have talked about this, but because the ratings weren't insane and because they weren't too bad, they basically left you guys alone to create your weird little show where you could use balance of action and not a surf and kind of create your own universe.
但你知道，我们经历的弧线，我认为发生的事情是——我想我们可能讨论过这个——因为收视率没有疯狂到极点，也没有太糟糕，他们基本上让你们自己去创作你们那部奇怪的小剧，你们可以在那里平衡动作和叙事，并创造你们自己的宇宙。

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:04.819
And I think if we had been too successful, I think they would have been around too much.
我想如果我们太成功了，他们可能会干预太多。

00:33:04.819 --> 00:33:05.819
I think that's right.
我想那是对的。

00:33:05.819 --> 00:33:09.579
And I think if we weren't successful, we wouldn't be talking right now.
而且我想如果我们不成功，我们现在就不会在这里谈话了。

00:33:09.579 --> 00:33:16.740
So I think there was a build that allowed us to get our voice and grow our audience.
所以我认为有一个积累的过程，让我们能够找到自己的声音并扩大观众群。

00:33:16.740 --> 00:33:27.912
You know, I have some friends who, you know, I have a friend who's very successful in another area of showbiz, but he was like, coming up is the best.
你知道，我有一些朋友，你知道，我有一个朋友在演艺圈的其他领域非常成功，但他当时说，上升期是最好的。

00:33:27.912 --> 00:33:30.519
He's like, being on top is not fun.
他说，站在顶峰并不好玩。

00:33:30.519 --> 00:33:38.730
He uses, I actually put this in a song lyric, but he said, when you get to the top of Everest, the air is so thin that your body actually starts to die.
他用过——我实际上把它写进了歌词里——他说，当你到达珠穆朗玛峰顶端时，空气稀薄到你的身体实际上开始死亡。

00:33:38.730 --> 00:33:43.267
That's why they have to get you up and down so quickly from the top of the mountain.
这就是为什么他们必须让你从山顶迅速上下来的原因。

00:33:43.267 --> 00:33:48.560
And he's like, that's what the top of showbiz is, like the air is so thin, your body starts dying.
他说，这就是演艺圈的顶峰，空气太稀薄了，你的身体开始死亡。

00:33:48.560 --> 00:33:53.799
So you got to go up and you got to collect your award and you got to come back down to real life.
所以你必须上去，领完奖，然后回到现实生活中。

00:33:53.799 --> 00:33:54.799
Yeah.
是的。

00:33:54.799 --> 00:33:55.799
I think that's right.
我想那是对的。

00:33:55.799 --> 00:33:56.799
I think in the end, it was a real gift.
